WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.892 --> 00:00:16.021
The and Mother stared at the dark house.

2
00:00:16.041 --> 00:00:20.304
"I wonder why the windows are closed.

3
00:00:21.485 --> 00:00:22.266
I asked Mrs.

4
00:00:22.326 --> 00:00:24.287
Viney to open them," Mother said.

5
00:00:25.268 --> 00:00:25.888
"Who's she?"

6
00:00:26.309 --> 00:00:26.929
asked Bobbie.

7
00:00:26.949 --> 00:00:30.892
"The woman I asked to clean and make some supper for us."

8
00:00:32.236 --> 00:00:33.597
They walked to the back of the house.

9
00:00:34.978 --> 00:00:38.160
The cart clattered onto the cobblestones and stopped at the back door.

10
00:00:39.982 --> 00:00:41.703
The children knocked but no one answered.

11
00:00:42.904 --> 00:00:44.325
The cart driver said that Mrs.

12
00:00:44.385 --> 00:00:45.786
Viney had probably gone home.

13
00:00:46.566 --> 00:00:48.188
The train had arrived very late.

14
00:00:48.208 --> 00:00:50.850
"But she has the key!"

15
00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:51.870
Mother said.

16
00:00:51.890 --> 00:00:56.974
"Oh, I'm sure she left it under the doorstep," the cart driver said.

17
00:00:56.994 --> 00:00:59.516
"That's what people do around here."

18
00:01:00.768 --> 00:01:02.969
He took the lantern off his cart and bent down.

19
00:01:02.989 --> 00:01:06.130
"Here it is, sure enough!"

20
00:01:07.151 --> 00:01:07.971
He unlocked the door.

21
00:01:10.452 --> 00:01:12.953
The cart driver put down his lantern and lit a candle.

22
00:01:13.874 --> 00:01:16.495
The kitchen was large, with a stone floor.

23
00:01:17.535 --> 00:01:18.596
The table was in the middle.

24
00:01:19.716 --> 00:01:23.638
The chairs, pots, pans, and crockery were in all corners of the room.

25
00:01:25.099 --> 00:01:27.460
There was no fire, just cold ashes.

26
00:01:28.572 --> 00:01:30.853
A rustling sound came from inside the walls.

27
00:01:30.873 --> 00:01:34.155
"Oh, what's that?"

28
00:01:34.515 --> 00:01:35.216
cried the girls.

29
00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:38.618
"It's only the rats," said the cart driver.

30
00:01:39.698 --> 00:01:42.940
He left and shut the door, and a sudden wind blew out the candle.

31
00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:49.363
"Oh dear," said Phyllis, "I wish we hadn't come!"

32
00:01:49.884 --> 00:01:51.104
And she knocked a chair over.

33
00:01:51.124 --> 00:01:53.445
"Only the rats!"

34
00:01:53.946 --> 00:01:54.986
said Peter in the dark.

35
00:01:56.127 --> 00:01:56.967
"What fun!"

36
00:01:57.428 --> 00:01:59.797
said Mother, feeling for the matches on the table.

37
00:01:59.817 --> 00:02:03.478
"I'm sure they are mice, not rats!"

38
00:02:04.979 --> 00:02:07.140
She struck a match and everyone looked at each other.

39
00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:13.663
"Well," Mother said, "you've often wanted something to happen and now it has.

40
00:02:14.583 --> 00:02:16.544
This is quite an adventure, isn't it?

41
00:02:17.665 --> 00:02:19.125
Let's go and eat the supper Mrs.

42
00:02:19.165 --> 00:02:19.906
Viney made."

43
00:02:21.386 --> 00:02:22.907
The dining room was next to the kitchen.

44
00:02:23.967 --> 00:02:24.808
The kitchen was white.

45
00:02:25.948 --> 00:02:28.829
But the dining room was made of dark wood from floor to ceiling.

46
00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:32.431
There was a table and chairs, but there was no supper.

47
00:02:32.451 --> 00:02:37.673
"Let's look in the other rooms," said Mother, and they looked.

48
00:02:38.814 --> 00:02:42.535
In each room there were furniture and boxes, but nothing to eat.

49
00:02:43.495 --> 00:02:45.916
Even in the pantry there was only a rusty cake tin.

50
00:02:45.936 --> 00:02:48.858
"What a horrible woman!"

51
00:02:49.298 --> 00:02:49.758
said Mother.

52
00:02:49.778 --> 00:02:54.100
"She's taken the money but got us nothing to eat at all!"

53
00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:58.923
"Then we can't have any supper," said Phyllis unhappily.

54
00:02:58.943 --> 00:03:02.065
"Yes, we can," said Mother.

55
00:03:02.085 --> 00:03:04.767
"We can unpack one of the boxes.

56
00:03:05.727 --> 00:03:07.368
There's some food from the old house."

57
00:03:09.170 --> 00:03:13.272
They were all very, very tired, but they cheered up at their unusual supper.

58
00:03:14.913 --> 00:03:18.316
There were biscuits, sardines, raisins, and jam.

59
00:03:19.696 --> 00:03:22.418
After supper they put sheets and blankets on the beds.

60
00:03:23.579 --> 00:03:25.532
"Good night, darlings," said Mother.

61
00:03:25.552 --> 00:03:28.834
"I'm sure there aren't any rats.

62
00:03:29.894 --> 00:03:33.815
But I'll leave my door open, and if a mouse comes, you can scream.

63
00:03:34.936 --> 00:03:36.957
I'll come and tell the mouse to go away!"

64
00:03:38.157 --> 00:03:41.038
Bobbie, Peter, and Phyllis were not convinced by her answer.

65
00:03:42.139 --> 00:03:45.500
They left candles burning and spent the first night in their new home.
